coder › Done. I added `src/redact.ts` with `redact(value)`, wired it into `log()` in `src/logger.ts`, and added tests for both.

What changed
- `src/redact.ts` (new): `redact(value)` returns a deep copy. It redacts, at any depth of plain objects and arrays:
  - any key containing `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization` (case-insensitive) → `'[redacted]'`
  - any string value with `Bearer <token>` → `Bearer [redacted]` (repeated occurrences too)
  - everything else is preserved; non-plain objects and primitives are returned as-is, and the input is never mutated.
- `src/logger.ts`: imports `redact` and spreads `redact(fields)` into the line instead of raw `fields`.
- `src/redact.test.ts` (new): covers non-mutation/copy, all sensitive key names and case variants, nested objects/arrays, bearer token replacement, and unchanged values.
- `src/logger.test.ts`: kept the original test and added cases for sensitive fields, bearer tokens, and nested fields.

Commits
- `b849c43` Add redact helper and pass logger fields through it
- `f8b0438` Test redact helper and logger redaction

